title: 'pallet-psm: reject the `None` origin as a PSM admin'
doc:
- audience: [Runtime Dev, Runtime User]
  description: |-
    A PSM admin could be set to the system `None` origin. The pool rejects unsigned PSM
    calls, but a block author bypasses the pool, so such a PSM would be managed by whoever
    authors the block.

    The `None` origin is now rejected both when storing an admin, via the new
    `Error::InvalidAdminOrigin`, and when checking one in `ensure_psm_admin`. The latter
    also covers admin records already in storage.
crates:
- name: pallet-psm
  bump: major
